      <room>H.1302</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Gumby</title>
      <subtitle>a package dependency Browser/Viewer for Linux</subtitle>
      <track>CrossDistro devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Data visualization has been in shortage in the area of Linux distros despite the abundance of package managers.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;With the honourable exception of debtree there is/was no way to visually explore a local package universe.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this talk I&amp;#39;ll talk about how Gumby can fit in the current package management landscape to help the user or package maintainer to visually inspect his current package universe.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="701">André Guerreiro</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>